 34SI    34AL B- DECAY:MIXED           2024LU03                  ENSDF    202609
 34SI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34SI c  2024LU03: {+34}Al ions were produced via reactions of a 480-MeV 14-|mA 
 34SI2c  proton beam impinging on a 9.89-g/cm{+2} UC{-x} target at ISAC, TRIUMF.
 34SI3c  The ions were selectively ionized using the TRIUMF Resonant Ionization 
 34SI4c  Laser Ion Source (TRILIS) and accelerated to 40 keV.                   


 The ions were separated by the ISAC mass separator and
 34SI4c  implanted to a mylar tape in the center of Gamma-Ray Infrastructure For
 34SI5c  Fundamental Investigation of Nuclei (GRIFFIN). The tape was moved      
 34SI6c  continuously at a speed of 1 cm/s in order to reduce the long-lived    
 34SI7c  descendants from the {+34}Al decay chain. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g,     
 34SI8c  |b|g, |g|g-coin. Deduced J, |p, |b-feeding, logft.                     
 34SI c  See Table II of 2024Lu03 for the authors deduction of beta-feedings    
 34SI2c  following their separation of intensities from each parent.            
 34SI cL E$From least chi-square fit to E|g's, unless otherwise stated.         
 34SI cG RI$Normalized to I|g(3226|g)=100.                                      
